<title>USA: U.S. House lawmakers slam nuke safety regulators.</title>
<headline>U.S. House lawmakers slam nuke safety regulators.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. House lawmakers on Thursday belatedly attacked federal regulators for letting safety lapses at nuclear plants go unchecked for many years, but praised Nuclear Regulator Commission chairman Shirley Jackson for taking steps to toughen enforcement.</p>
<p>In its first hearing in five years on nuclear safety, the House energy and power panel questioned whether the commission was doing its job, doing enough to shield workers from retaliation when they alleged there were safety problems, and punishing agency staff who failed to report or pursue  violations.</p>
</text>
